  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "card": "An indexed eccentric cam: turn to raise or lower its guided follower.",
    "cam": "eccentric cam",
    "follower": "cam follower",
    "stroke": "indexed stroke model",
    "wrong_phase": "Choose the turn offer matching the current cam phase.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free to turn the shaft knob.",
    "howto_turn": "Use the forward or backward offer for the current phase. The cam indexes 22.5 degrees per step; its circular profile has a 220 mm radius and its center is offset 70 mm from the shaft. The guided follower follows the upper profile at the shaft centerline, highest at phase zero and lowest at phase eight: a 140 mm indexed stroke. One phase drives both cam and follower, so there is no independent follower setting. Forward moves the cam center initially toward positive x, using negative picture Z rotation. This is an indexed pose exhibit, not force, spring, torque, load, collision, smooth-wrap, continuous-contact or material-working simulation."
  },
